# HDO-derived paths, read by pr-gate run (scripts/pr-gate-lane).
# HDO model transcripts and their outputs never reach a non-HDO account or a non-Claude agent. A
# non-anthropic/ model is refused on a PR that changes any path below for its repo, and otherwise
# runs in a checkout of the PR head with these paths left out.
# Sami rules on what belongs here; the BET task-pipeline lane (PIPE) names BET's paths.
# One <owner>/<repo>:<glob> per line, repo-relative: `**` crosses directories, `*` does not, and
# `dir/**` covers dir itself. A machine's absolute paths (lane checkouts, run outputs) go in its
# untracked ~/.config/pr-gate/hdo-paths.local in the same form; a non-Claude gate on a repo listed
# here refuses to run without that file.

